Description: Fit, summarize, and predict for spatial linear and generalized linear models on stream networks. Stream covariance models use moving average constructions based on in-stream distance. Parameters are estimated using likelihood methods. Additional modeling features include Euclidean covariance, anisotropy, non-spatial random effects, partition factors, and big data methods. Model-fit statistics are used to summarize, visualize, and compare models, and predictions at unobserved locations are readily obtainable. For additional details, see Ver Hoef and Peterson (2010) <DOI:10.1198/jasa.2009.ap08248> and Dumelle et al. (2024) <DOI:10.21105/joss.06389>.
